{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Network Copilot Knowledge Files.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Network Copilot Knowledge Files.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"network copilot knowledge files network copilot knowledge files","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Network Copilot Knowledge Files.md","fileName":"Network Copilot Knowledge Files.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Network Copilot Knowledge Files","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Network Copilot Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network Copilot Design","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Network Copilot Knowledge Files.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Network Copilot Knowledge Files.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"network copilot knowledge files network copilot knowledge files","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Network Copilot Knowledge Files.md","fileName":"Network Copilot Knowledge Files.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Network Copilot Knowledge Files","heading":"Network Copilot Knowledge Files","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Network copilot knowledge files provide bounded local facts that a general model does not possess. Separate JSON files can describe device inventories, network context, known response examples, and topology relationships in forms that ordinary code can inspect before building a prompt.\n\nSeparation makes each source replaceable and reviewable, but filenames do not establish truth. Every file needs a defined owner, schema, update time, and validation path. The copilot should load only the subset relevant to the active device and intent so context remains focused.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network Copilot Design","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd